n b12 or b9 is low there's usually  a decrease in a number of circulating  antibodies as well thus the body will be  exposed to a large number of infections  and the capability of quickly recovering  from infections will diminish foods like  avocados strawberry and banana are very  rich in vitamin B while other foods like  dairy products such as yogurt or milk  also have it in sufficient quantities to  add variety eat vegetables like  asparagus as well as meat and fish in  order to have enough vitamin B in your  diet  perhaps vitamin C is one vitamin you are  most familiar with because it has been  used since ages to boost immunity and  decrease the duration of colds and flu  vitamin C also called the ascorbic acid  is an essential micronutrients for  humans and one of the most widely  consumed dietary supplements in the  world  vitamin C increases the production of  interferons a protein which helps the  immune cells to fight viral infections  many research groups have suggested the  importance of vitamin C indeed and it is  still considered one of the best  vitamins to promote a strong immune  system it boosts our immunity in many  other ways which we have discussed in  detail in our next video which will be  about the role of vitamin C in  strengthening our immunity check the  links in the description bar below for  more details  vitamin C can be found in citrus fruits  like oranges and lemons as well as other  fruits like blackberries guava Kiwi and  strawberries nevertheless between C can  also be found in huge quantities in  other vegetables like red bell peppers  try mixing up your sources to eat  different foods in every meal  our next immune system boosting vitamin  is the vitamin E vitamin E helps the  immune system because of its antioxidant  properties it helps fight free radicals  and helps ourselves to regenerate and  work seamlessly  it can be found in walnuts almonds  peanuts and it is also found in  sunflower seeds spinach and broccoli the  best oils that have this vitamin are the  sunflower oil wheat germ oil and soybean  oil  vitamin K is an essential fire soluble  vitamin involved in heart and bone  health however it is also among the best  vitamins for the immune system health  vitamin K acts as a cofactor for many  plasma proteins and strengthens our  innate immunity vitamin K that we  absorbed from our diet is related to  intestinal bacteria therefore the blood  vitamin K levels greatly depend upon our  digestive health  this video features five of the best  vitamins for immune system health  including vitamin A vitamin B vitamin C  vitamin E and vitamin K we also explain  how each vitamin benefits the immune  system as well as which foods are rich  in these vitamins a vitamin rich diet  will be heavy in fruits vegetables and  other whole foods when you do supplement  with vitamins it is best to choose a  high-quality product made from real food  sources and free from fillers or toxins  I recommend Nature's Way multivitamin  supplements which contains all the  vitamins that we just discussed and also  has loads of other micronutrients which  gives boost to the five essential  aspects of a healthy immunity which is  cellular immunity circulatory immunity  digestive immunity respiratory immunity  as well as systemic immunity links are  in the description bar below if you're  one of those who is not into taking  vitamin pills check out this video about  the top 10 foods that you can include in  your diet to boost your immunity thank  you so much and see you in the next  video bye-bye take care and stay safe  thank you so much for watching
 

